When a seccomp filter outside PRoot's control (Android's app policy)
traps a syscall with SIGSYS, answer it with -ENOSYS instead of letting
the signal kill the tracee, so callers run their fallback for syscalls
the platform doesn't allow (io_uring, clone3, epoll_pwait2, rseq, ...).
faccessat2 with no flag besides AT_EACCESS is re-issued as faccessat
(arm64), which keeps access checks exact.

